WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.880
[music]

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:08.480
Google Cloud Vision is a powerful image analysis tool delivered through an intuitive API.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.220
Cloud Vision recognizes and understands a broad set of entities inside of an image.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:19.080
It can read text, human emotions, and even knows that this mango is with high confidence a mango.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.520
But at Google, we take moonshots. So we thought: could these APIs do more?

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.740
The idea came one day when Miles said to me . . .

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.840
Michele, does this look too normcore to you?

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.540
And I...I had no idea.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:39.180
Today, we’re sharing the newest feature of the Cloud Vision API: Style Detection.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:44.420
Now, Vision can tell you not what clothes you’re wearing, but what that might say about you.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:50.320
Imagine fashion based on data, not feelings. That would be a better dressed world.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.620
[music]

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.220
We knew we needed experts for this project.

00:00:55.220 --> 00:01:00.960
So we invited fashion consultants even elite teenage bloggers to help us figure this out.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:06.960
Style is intangible, enigmatic even. It’s not just about patterns or pleats or when to wear white.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:12.740
Style is an art, it's an instinct. Can it be taught? Uhh, I don’t know.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.940
There’s eco chic and boho chic and geek chic…

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:18.820
Fuzzy. Goth. Hyper-goth. Those are good.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:20.920
There’s a whole chic list!

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:26.640
Like humans, teaching machines takes time. And the larger the training corpus, the better our predictions will be.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.880
We’ve analyzed millions of images. A-line skirts, fedoras, you name it.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:38.040
Our mantra here at Google is to launch early and iterate. So that’s exactly what we did on this project.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:41.040
[music]

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:47.300
We set up a live testing environment in order to analyze  [hairspray spraying] an even more diverse set of personal styles.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:56.680
We made adjustments when needed and fine-tuned the algorithm as our training corpus continued to grow.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:06.580
[music]

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:14.460
We discovered that fashion exists, not just in the streets, but in the clouds. This is a new beginning in fashion history.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:19.540
We’re excited to bring Style Detection to the world. Because fashion touches all of us.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:25.460
You only get a few chances to make a first impression. Sign up for the alpha today.

